 QQQ: Are the above parameters correct (Y/n)?: yes!

 The maximum sizes of sources and filaments need to be manually (visually)   
 estimated from prepared images before an extraction, for each waveband      
 independently. This can be done by opening an image in DS9 and placing a    
 circular region with a certain angular radius over the largest structure.   

 The maximum sizes are defined as the footprint radii of the largest source  
 and the widest filament of interest. A footprint is defined as the full     
 width of a structure at zero (background) level, i.e., the largest extent   
 on both sides from the source peak or filament crest, where that structure  
 is still visible against its background.                                    

 Separated background of the filamentary component must be inspected to      
 verify that there are no residuals. If residuals of the filaments appear    
 clearly visible, the background is not accurate for filament measurements.  
 The maximum size of the filaments of interest in the config file must be    
 increased and a new extraction of the filaments must be started.            

